          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The term
            %em stratified space
            usually refers to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            equipped with the structure of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stratification"} stratification
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+subspaces"} topological subspaces
            called
            = succeed "." do
              %em strata
          %p
            Often strata are required to be “nice” in some sense (for instance, one may require strata to be
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces"} spaces
            equipped with some type of stratification structure.
          %p
            Examples are ubiquitous, canonical stratifications are carried by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polyhedra"} polyhedra
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cell+complexes"} cell complexes
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+varieties"} algebraic varieties
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+spaces"} orbit spaces
            of many
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+actions"} group actions
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cylinders"} mapping cylinders
            of maps between manifolds, and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stacks+of+formal+groups"} moduli stacks of formal groups
            (stratified by
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/height+of+a+formal+group"} height of formal groups
          %h2#variants Variants
          %p There are many different definitions of stratifications on spaces:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                stratifications from
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+topological+space"} filtrations
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset-stratified+space"}> poset-stratifications
                ,
            %li
              %p
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Whitney stratifications
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Whitney+stratifications"} ?
                (cf. the
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whitney_conditions"} Wikipedia
            %li
              %p
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Thom-Mather stratifications
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Thom-Mather+stratifications"} ?
                (see e.g.
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thom%E2%80%93Mather_stratified_space"} Wiki entry
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stratifold"}> stratifolds
                ,
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"}> orbifolds
                ,
            %li
              %p
                homotopical stratifications (as developed by
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a{:href => "#Quinn"} Quinn
            %li
              %p
                conically smooth stratifications (as developed by
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a{:href => "#AFT"} Ayala-Francis-Tanaka
            %li
              %p etc. …
          %h2#basic_features Basic features
          %h3#StratificationStructures Stratification structures
          %p Most of the above variants share the same basic structure, captured by the following definitions.
          %p
          #ExitPathPreorder.num_defn
            %h6 Terminology
            %p
              %strong (exit path preorder)
              %br/
              Given a decomposition
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              into
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+space"} connected
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace#topological_subspaces"} subspaces
              (denoted, in the following, by lower-case letters such as
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              %em exit path preorder
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Exit
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{Exit}(f)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preorder"} preorder
              of subspaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              with a generating arrow
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo →
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \to r
              whenever the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+closure"} topological closure
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              intersects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              non-trivially.
          %p
          #Stratification.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong stratification
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a decomposition of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Exit
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{Exit}(f)
              (Trm.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExitPathPreorder"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
          %p
            The subspaces in a stratification are also called
            = succeed "." do
              %em strata
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite
            poset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi Exit
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{Exit}(f)^{\mathrm{op}}
            is also called the
            %em entrance path poset
            and denoted by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Entr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{Entr}(f)
          %p
          #CharacteristicMap.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (characteristic map)
              %br/
              Given a stratification
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Exit
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \mathrm{Exit}(f)
              mapping points
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in s
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Exit
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \in \mathrm{Exit}(f)
              %strong characteristic map
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Exit
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to \mathrm{Exit}(f)
          %p
            The characteristic map (Rmk.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CharacteristicMap"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous
            in general (unless the stratification is locally finite, see Rmk
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ContinuityOfCharacteristicMap"}
            below); it is, however, continuous on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimage"} preimage
            of any finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+functor"} full
            subposet of the exit path poset. It is often convenient to construct stratifications by constructing their characteristic map.
          %p
          #CWStratification.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (Stratification of CW complexes)
              %br/
              The following are stratifications of the 1- and 2-spheres:
              %img{:alt => "", :src => "/nlab/files/SphereStratification.jpg"}/
            %p
              In general, a stratification of a CW complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is obtained by taking the strata to be the
              = succeed "-cells" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (for each
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "-skeleton" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{n-1}
              removed.
          %p
          #PosetStratification.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (Poset stratifications)
              %br/
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to P
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
              (in other words,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset-stratified+space"}
                  stratification of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{c}(f)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (in the sense of Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Stratification"}
              above) whose strata are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimages"} preimages
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(x)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in P
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              factors uniquely through the characteristic map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Exit
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{c}(f) \colon X \to \mathsf{Exit}(\mathrm{c}(f))
              by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conservative+functor"} conservative
              poset map
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                        %mi Exit
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{Exit}(\mathrm{c}(f)) \to P
          %p The example shows that any poset-stratification determines a unique stratification. However, many poset-stratifications may determine the same stratification in this way.
          %p
          #FilteredSpaces.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (Filtered spaces)
              Any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+topological+space"} filtered topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0 \subset X_1 \subset ... \subset X_n
              in which each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_i
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subspace"} closed subspace
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{i+1}
              defines a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo →
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to [n] = (0 \to 1 \to ... \to n)
              mapping points in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ∖
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{i+1} \setminus X_{i}
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PosetStratification"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cell+complex"} cell complex
              defines the “stratification by cells” in this way.
          %p
          #TrivialStratification.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (Trivial stratification)
              %br/
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is trivially stratified (in the sense of Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Stratification"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          %p
          #ContinuityOfCharacteristicMap.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (Continuity of characteristic map)
              %br/
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,f)
              be a stratified space according to Def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Stratification"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is “locally finite” if each stratum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              has an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighborhood"} open neighborhood
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              which only contains finitely many strata. (If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,f)
              satisfies the frontier condition (Rmk.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FrontierCondition"}
              below) then, equivalently,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,f)
              is locally finite iff each point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              has an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighborhood"} open neighborhood
              intersecting only finitely many strata.) If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is locally finite, then the characteristic map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Exit
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to \mathsf{Exit}(f)
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CharacteristicMap"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
          %p
          #FrontierCondition.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (Openness of characteristic map)
              %br/
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,f)
              be a stratified space (Def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Stratification"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              satisfies the “frontier condition” (or, as an adjective, that it is “frontier-constructible”) if, for any two strata
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ,
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s, r
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+closure"} topological closure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi r
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline r
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              non-trivially, then
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
